  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nDry conditions are expected through Friday. Low pressure in the Great\nLakes will see disturbances cross the northern Ohio Valley, bringing\nthe next round of showers and thunderstorms to the region. This low\nwill evolve into a l/w trough extending from the Great lakes\nsouthwest to MO/AR on Saturday. By Sunday evening, what is expected\nto be a thin and quite elongated trough will see its axis cross the\nCWA, bringing an end to a sometimes rainy weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nNear normal temperatures are expected for daytime highs with warmer \nthan normal overnight lows. CAA will still be found today, resulting\nin some afternoon cloudiness with fair wx cu. Temperatures will drop\ninto the 70s Saturday, near 80 on Sunday with cloud cover and rain.\nReadings will return to near normal for highs and above normal on\nlows for next week.",
